Description: Identifies genes whose expression changes along single-cell
    pseudotime and differs between the branching paths of a trajectory. Cells
    are pseudo-bulked into pseudotime bins that preserve their ordering, and
    the polynomial generalised linear model of the 'maSigPro' package is
    fitted to the binned counts with a negative binomial family and
    size-factor offsets. Methods are described in Srivastava et al. (2024)
    <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btae443>.
